{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A Psalm of Asaph. Only good</b> — all the children of man who do not understand the deed of HaShem in truth, they complain; and on account of this he began אך טוב לישראל, for the meaning of אך is that it is not good for the nations of the lands who do not know Him, only to Israel." "<b>To the pure of heart</b> — not to all. This psalm resembles in its meaning the psalm Hear this, all you peoples, and the reward of the righteous in the world to come is explicitly stated in this psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:05.172892528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}